interlock_runtime borrows designs, not code, from these projects. Nothing is vendored.

- Absurd (earendil-works/absurd, Apache-2.0): SKIP LOCKED claims with takeover on an expired lease,
  the database clock for timers and leases, eager fencing of stale writers.
- DBOS Transact (dbos-inc, MIT): steps keyed by call order, fork of a workflow at a step,
  first-writer-wins recording of decisions.
- Temporal (temporalio, MIT): retry policy defaults (initial 1s, backoff 2.0, max interval 100x initial,
  unlimited attempts), patched() semantics, loud non-determinism.
- Restate (restatedev, design only; server is BSL 1.1 and is not used): pinning a running workflow to
  the code version it started on.

Dependency: psycopg (psycopg/psycopg) is LGPL-3.0. It is imported unmodified as a separate package,
which the LGPL permits without affecting this package's license.

Receipts and the effect journal format come from the interlock package in this repository (MIT).
